        "original_id": "3c87b20b-f8be-5be9-aaa2-ee413ebf8207",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ara Berberian, Giuseppe Verdi, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\n- Works: Rigoletto, The Abduction from the Seraglio\n- Roles: Osmin, Sparafucile\n- Topics: Opera, musical performance\n\nFacts:\n- Ara Berberian was born on May 14, 1930, in Detroit, Michigan.\n- Ara Berberian was an American bass and actor with an active international career in operas, concerts, and musicals from the early 1960s until his retirement from the stage in 1997.\n- Ara Berberian sang more than 100 roles during his career.\n- Ara Berberian performed the role of Osmin in Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart's The Abduction from the Seraglio.\n- Giuseppe Verdi's Rigoletto is an opera in three acts.\n- Ara Berberian performed the role of Sparafucile in Giuseppe Verdi's Rigoletto.\n- Ara Berberian died on February 21, 2005, in Boynton Beach, Florida.",
